-- title:
--   Complete Nakayama surjection onto a completed node ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, together with modular polynomial data for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at $(j,j_q)$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ on the Hecke operators $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$ at level $N$ and prime $q$, a place specialization $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$; assume $k$ perfect. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $K$ finite over $\mathbb Q$, put $A_0 := A \cap K$ (the intersection of $A$ with $K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), let $w$ be a place of the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ over $k$, and let $c$ be a system of node coordinates for $R$ over $K$ at $w$: elements $x, y$ of the ring $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ (those elements of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegers}\ w$ whose Laurent expansion lies in the field $\mathrm{fieldOver}\ (Nq)\ K$) with first residue of $x$ zero, the order of the second residue of $x$ at the Frobenius translate $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\ q\ k\ N \cdot w$ equal to $1$, second residue of $y$ zero, and $w$-order of the first residue of $y$ equal to $1$. Let $\varpi \in A_0$ be such that an element $d$ of $A_0$ reduces to $0$ under the restriction of $red$ to $A_0$ precisely when $d$ is a multiple of $\varpi$. Assume $R_w := R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ is local and Noetherian, that its maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the constant $\varpi$ (the image of $\varpi$ under the constant-embedding homomorphism $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\ K\ w : A_0 \to R_w$) together with $c.x$ and $c.y$, and that every $g \in R_w$ admits an $o \in A_0$ with $g - \mathrm{nodeConst}\ o$ a non-unit. Writing $W := A_0[[T]]/(T - \varpi)$, the conclusion asserts the existence of ring homomorphisms $\theta_W : W \to \widehat{R_w}$ and $\theta : W[[X_0,X_1]] \to \widehat{R_w}$ into the $\mathfrak m_{R_w}$-adic completion of $R_w$ such that $\theta_W$ sends the class of the constant series $o$ to the image of $\mathrm{nodeConst}\ o$ for every $o \in A_0$ and the class of $T$ to the image of $\mathrm{nodeConst}\ \varpi$, the coefficient inclusion followed by $\theta$ equals $\theta_W$, $\theta(X_0)$ and $\theta(X_1)$ are the images of $c.x$ and $c.y$, and $\theta$ is surjective.
--
--   This is the complete Nakayama, or $\mathfrak m$-adic approximation, step at a supersingular node: a complete local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\varpi$ and two node coordinates, and whose residue field is generated by the constants from $A_0 = A \cap K$, is a quotient of the two-variable power series ring over the completion $W$ of $A_0$. It is obtained from the general surjectivity criterion [`IsLocalRing.exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_adicCompletion_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_adicCompletion_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span), the structure of $A_0$ given by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.coeffSubring_eq_or_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.coeffSubring_eq_or_isDiscreteValuationRing), and the description of $W$ in [`PowerSeries.quotient_span_X_sub_C_pow_of_irreducible`](thm.html#PowerSeries.quotient_span_X_sub_C_pow_of_irreducible); it is used in the rows computing residues and slope drops at the node of $X_0(Nq)$.
